IMPORT prelude

-- School Boards (Incorporation) Act 1990 (Singapore) -- what a school's governing board is and may do, and what happens to the people
-- who deal with it: aided schools and the founder's consent (ss 2, 7), the full discretion an order may give a board over staff,
-- admissions and fees (s 3(4)(h), (i)), varying a constitution (s 4), the common seal and proof of documents (s 6), the protection of
-- governors from personal liability (s 8), discontinuing a school (s 9), the Minister's takeover through the Director-General
-- (s 10), winding up (s 11), and deemed registration of schools and managers under the Education Act 1957 (ss 13, 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SBIA1990.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021. Its Legislative
-- History lists only Act 4 of 1990 and the 1991 and 2013 Revised Editions: no amending Act is annotated.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0202 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (16 sections) and the row covers most of it. Not encoded: the incorporation mechanics and the
-- contents of a constitution beyond s 3(4)(h) and (i) (s 3(1)-(5), (7)), the list of powers in s 5, the contents of a winding-up
-- order (s 11(2)), grants (s 12), the saving for the Education Act 1957 (s 15) and transfers of property (s 16). The Act creates no
-- offence and no penalty. No order made under s 3(1) was retrieved, so what any actual school board may do is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `School Boards (Incorporation) Act 1990 -- governing boards`

§§ `2 and 7 -- aided schools and the founder's consent`

-- s 2: "aided school" means a school which "(a) is established by any person other than the Government; and (b) is conducted by a
-- committee of management which is in receipt of a grant-in-aid from the Government for defraying the expenses incurred for
-- conducting the school".
-- s 7: "The Minister must not establish a governing board for the purpose of conducting an aided school unless the person or body of
-- persons which established the aided school agrees".
-- s 7 is the only limit the text sets on the s 3(1) power. That a Government school needs no one's consent is an INFERENCE from
-- that silence; the long title confines the Act to "Government schools and aided schools".
GIVEN `established by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `conducted by a management committee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the committee receives a grant-in-aid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school is an aided school` IF
    (NOT `established by the Government`) AND `conducted by a management committee` AND `the committee receives a grant-in-aid`

GIVEN `established by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `conducted by a management committee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the committee receives a grant-in-aid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the founder agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may establish a governing board` IF
        (NOT `the school is an aided school` `established by the Government` `conducted by a management committee` `the committee receives a grant-in-aid`)
    OR  `the founder agrees`

§§ `3(4)(h), (i) -- what an order may hand to the board`

-- s 3(4): an order "may make provisions" ... "(h) conferring upon the governing board full discretion to act with respect to the
-- following matters: (i) the recruitment, promotion and dismissal of and the exercise of disciplinary control over teachers and other
-- staff of the school; (ii) determining the policy or conditions for the admission of pupils to the school and the dismissal of
-- pupils; (iii) determining the fees payable by the pupils of the school"; "(i) to allow the governing board to retain the fees
-- collected from the pupils".
-- The Act itself gives the board none of these: each depends on what the order says. s 3(4) opens "Without limiting subsection (1)",
-- so an order might reach other matters; the rule below says only whether the matter is one s 3(4)(h) LISTS.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `hiring and dismissing teachers`
    `disciplining staff`
    `admitting pupils`
    `dismissing pupils`
    `setting school fees`
    `the school curriculum`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(4)(h) lists the matter` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `the school curriculum` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter, `the order confers full discretion over it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board has full discretion under s 3(4)(h)` IF
    `s 3(4)(h) lists the matter` `the matter` AND `the order confers full discretion over it`

GIVEN `the order allows the board to retain fees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board may keep the fees it collects` IF
    `the order allows the board to retain fees`

§§ `4 -- varying a constitution`

-- s 4: the constitution "may be varied or revoked by the Minister, but before varying or revoking the constitution and making a new
-- constitution for any governing board, the Minister must consult the governing board concerned." Consult, not obtain consent.
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the board` IS A BOOLEAN, `the board objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may vary the constitution` IF
    `the Minister consulted the board`

§§ `6 -- the common seal and proof of documents`

-- s 6(1): the seal "may only be affixed to an instrument or document in the presence of any 2 persons, being governors, that the
-- governing board determines, or in the absence of any such determination, in the presence of 2 governors, who must sign the
-- instrument". Reading "2" as "at least 2" is an INFERENCE.
-- s 6(2): a document purporting to be executed under the seal, or signed by a person authorised by the board, "must be received in
-- evidence and be treated, without further proof, as being so made or issued unless the contrary is shown".
GIVEN `governors present` IS A NUMBER, `the board has designated sealing governors` IS A BOOLEAN, `those present are the designated governors` IS A BOOLEAN, `they signed the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seal is properly affixed` IF
        `governors present` >= 2
    AND `they signed the instrument`
    AND (    (NOT `the board has designated sealing governors`)
         OR  `those present are the designated governors`)

GIVEN `purports to be sealed or signed by an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is treated as the board's without further proof` IF
    `purports to be sealed or signed by an authorised person` AND (NOT `the contrary is shown`)

§§ `8 -- governors are not personally liable`

-- s 8: "Except as provided in this Act, no governor shall, by virtue merely of his or her holding that office -- (a) be liable to
-- contribute towards the payment of the debts and liabilities incurred in the conduct of a school or the costs ... of a winding up";
-- "(b) be conferred with any right, title or interest ... in the property of the governing board, and no suit or other legal
-- proceedings shall lie personally against that governor for anything which is in good faith done or intended to be done in the
-- conduct of a school or in the execution or purported execution of this Act."
GIVEN `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the conduct of the school or purported execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a suit lies personally against the governor` IF
    NOT (`acted in good faith` AND `in the conduct of the school or purported execution of the Act`)

GIVEN `liable only because a governor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the governor must contribute to the board's debts` IF
    NOT `liable only because a governor`

§§ `9 -- discontinuing a school`

-- s 9(1): the board "must not discontinue the school except in pursuance of proposals approved by the Director-General"; (2) after a
-- resolution at a meeting it must submit its proposals "as soon as practicable"; (3) the Director-General may reject them or approve
-- them "with or without modifications".
GIVEN `the board resolved at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN, `proposals were submitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Director-General approved them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board may discontinue the school` IF
    `the board resolved at a meeting` AND `proposals were submitted` AND `the Director-General approved them`

§§ `10 -- the Minister's takeover through the Director-General`

-- s 10(1): where the Minister "is satisfied that the governing board of a school has failed to conduct the school efficiently or that
-- the education of the pupils of the school is not being promoted in a proper manner", the Minister may appoint the Director-General
-- to exercise the board's powers for the period the Minister specifies.
-- (2): not unless the Minister "has given not less than 90 days' notice in writing to the chairperson", and "the chairperson may make
-- representations to the Minister within 60 days of the service of the notice".
-- (3): while the order stands no governor may exercise a power the Director-General is authorised to exercise.
-- (4): the Director-General's costs "are to be paid out of the funds of the governing board".
-- Day arithmetic below (day of service plus 60; plus 90) is an INFERENCE about how the periods are counted.
GIVEN `failed to conduct the school efficiently` IS A BOOLEAN, `education not promoted properly` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice was in writing to the chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may appoint the Director-General` IF
        (`failed to conduct the school efficiently` OR `education not promoted properly`)
    AND `notice was in writing to the chairperson`
    AND `days of notice given` >= 90

GIVEN `day the notice is served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last day for representations` IS
    `day the notice is served` PLUS 60

GIVEN `day the notice is served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the earliest day for the takeover order` IS
    `day the notice is served` PLUS 90

GIVEN `a takeover order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order covers the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a governor may exercise the power` IF
    NOT (`a takeover order is in force` AND `the order covers the power`)

DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the governing board's funds`
    `the Government`
    `the governors personally`

GIVETH A Payer
DECIDE `who pays the Director-General's costs` IS
    `the governing board's funds`

§§ `11 -- winding up`

-- s 11(1): where "(a) any proposals by a governing board of a school have been approved under section 9; (b) the registration of the
-- school concerned under the Education Act 1957 is cancelled; or (c) the conduct of a school has been taken over by the
-- Director-General under section 10 for a period exceeding 12 months", the Minister may by order in the Gazette wind up the board.
-- (2)(c): the order may require the board to give its employees notice terminating their contracts from a date specified.
GIVEN `discontinuance proposals approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `registration cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `months under the Director-General` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may wind up the governing board` IF
        `discontinuance proposals approved`
    OR  `registration cancelled`
    OR  `months under the Director-General` > 12

§§ `13, 14 -- deemed registration under the Education Act 1957`

-- s 13: every school conducted by a governing board "is deemed to be registered under the provisions of the Education Act 1957 from
-- the date of incorporation of the governing board".
-- s 14: "every governor is deemed to be a registered manager of a school as from the date of his or her appointment as a governor."
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `day of incorporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school is deemed registered` IF
    `the day` >= `day of incorporation`

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `day of appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the governor is deemed a registered manager` IF
    `the day` >= `day of appointment`
